<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Birchas HaMazon U'Mayim Acharonim — Halachah 4<br>Part 3b (§§ 20–24) — FINAL<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">COMPLETE · Based on <span class="lr">LM II:40</span></span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 20 — <i>Ratzon</i> Is the Essential <i>Avodah</i>; <i>Birchas HaZimun</i></div>

<div class="p">Let us return to <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>. The essential <span class="h">mitzvah</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> is to reveal and draw the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> — <span class="v">"and you shall eat and be satisfied and bless Hashem your G-d for the good land."</span> This holiness is drawn through the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> revealed at the table — the cup of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>, as explained above at length. This is <span class="h">Birchas HaZimun</span> — when three are present, they say <span class="v">"let us bless [the One] from Whose [bounty] we have eaten"</span> before <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> — inviting [<span class="h">mezamnin</span>] themselves to bless.</div>

<div class="p">The matter is: the essential holiness and <span class="h">avodah</span> of the Jewish person is only the <span class="h">ratzon</span> and <span class="h">kisufin</span> of holiness, as explained in many places in Rabbainu's words. As he said: to serve Hashem — no one can boast that he can serve Him. Even an angel, even a <span class="h">seraph</span>, cannot boast of this. The essential thing is the <span class="h">ratzon</span> and <span class="h">kisufin</span> — one must exert oneself to always have strong desires and great yearnings for Hashem's service. (As this teaching is explained somewhat at the end of <span class="h">Sipurai Ma'asiyos</span>.) And more than this we heard from his holy mouth regarding the greatness of holy <span class="h">ratzon</span>, which is the essential <span class="h">avodas Hashem</span>. All <span class="h">avodos</span> — Torah, prayer, <span class="h">mitzvos</span>, good deeds — are all included in this. It is impossible to merit anything holy except through <span class="h">ratzon</span>, desire, yearning, <span class="h">kisufin</span>, and pining. One must never weaken the <span class="h">ratzon</span> in any way. The more the obstacle grows, one should strengthen oneself with ever stronger desire and <span class="h">kisufin</span> and <span class="h">ratzonos</span> — until one brings it from potential to actuality. As explained in <span class="v">"Vihi Na Pi Shenayim"</span> (<span class="lr">Siman 66</span>): the obstacle exists only for the desire. If one strengthens one's desire to match the obstacle, one will certainly break it.</div>

<div class="p">It emerges: the essential strengthening to overcome obstacles is only <span class="h">ratzon</span> and desire. This is the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — from Israel's <span class="h">azus</span> and stubbornness, through which Torah was received. The essential stubbornness is in <span class="h">ratzon</span>. One must be a great stubborn person in <span class="h">ratzon</span> — never abandoning, never weakening it through any obstacle. This is the essential holy stubbornness. This is the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>. For in truth, the <span class="h">avodah</span> itself is not so precious — everything is from Him: <span class="v">"who has preceded Me that I should repay?"</span> We cannot do anything holy without His help: <span class="mx">"every day the yetzer overpowers, and were it not that Hashem helps, he would fall."</span> Therefore the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is in the <span class="h">ratzon</span> — that each Jew desires with a strong <span class="h">ratzon</span> to serve Him.</div>

<div class="p">Even if one is the greatest stubborn person, there are certainly unbreakable obstacles — imprisonment, illness, and the like. Similarly regarding traveling to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>: if the sea stands before him with no ship, no money, or it is wartime — what good is stubbornness? One cannot jump into the sea; not everyone merits that Hashem split it for him. Therefore the essential stubbornness is only in <span class="h">ratzon</span> — come what may, never weaken the <span class="h">ratzon</span>. Even with thousands of seemingly unbreakable obstacles, one should do one's part and desire with ever stronger <span class="h">ratzon</span> — for the desire must match the obstacle (<span class="lr">Siman 66</span>). If one is a great stubborn person in <span class="h">ratzon</span>, never abandoning the <span class="h">kisufin</span> no matter how far one falls <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span> — then ultimately Hashem will certainly help break and nullify all obstacles, provide everything needed for the journey to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> or any holy matter, and turn things to good. For the obstacle existed only for the desire — the essential test being whether one abandons the <span class="h">ratzon</span>. When one stands firm and never abandons it, the obstacles transform into salvations.</div>

<div class="p">It emerges: the essential stubbornness is in <span class="h">ratzon</span>. This is the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>. This is <span class="v">"set me as a seal upon your heart, as a seal upon your arm, for love is as strong as death"</span> — <span class="v">"as a seal upon your heart, upon your arm"</span> is the aspect of <span class="h">tefillin</span>, as stated in the holy Zohar. <span class="h">Tefillin</span> are the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — Hashem takes pride in Israel and sets them as a seal upon His heart. The essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> that forms this seal of <span class="h">tefillin</span> is made through the love, yearning, <span class="h">ratzon</span>, and <span class="h">kisufin</span> of Israel. <span class="v">"Set me as a seal"</span> — <span class="h">tefillin</span>, <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — <span class="v">"for love is as strong as death"</span> — our love and <span class="h">ratzon</span> for You is fierce and strong with great <span class="h">azus</span> and stubbornness. Therefore it is fitting for You to take pride in us, for this is the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Love is as strong as death, jealousy as hard as the grave."</span> Love — <span class="h">ratzon</span> and desire and yearning for Hashem — through which the essential overcoming of the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>, which is the side of death, from which all obstacles come. According to the <span class="h">Sitra Achra's</span> strengthening, so must one's love and <span class="h">ratzon</span> be strong — the desire must match the obstacle. <span class="v">"Love is as strong as death"</span> — as strong as the obstacles from the side of death. <span class="v">"Hard as the grave"</span> — even if the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> fells one to the lowest depths <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span>, and one has no power to escape — if one is still a stubborn person in <span class="h">ratzon</span>, never abandoning it, yearning ever more for Hashem, with ever stronger <span class="h">ratzon</span> the more one falls — then Hashem has great <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> from this. For the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is the <span class="h">azus</span> and stubbornness of <span class="h">ratzon</span>. Through this one will ultimately accomplish what one desires — to draw close to Hashem.</div>

<div class="p">As it is written: <span class="v">"though You crushed us in the place of jackals and covered us in the shadow of death — if we had forgotten the Name of our G-d or spread our hands to a foreign god... for He knows the secrets of the heart — for Your sake we are killed all day long."</span> This is said regarding the exertions one makes for prayer or other holy matters — even though one has not yet merited to pray properly or accomplish what one desires, the exertion alone — the yearning and toil for it — is itself the aspect of <span class="h">korbanos</span>: <span class="v">"for Your sake we are killed all day long,"</span> as explained in Rabbainu's words. Therefore we ask Hashem: through the merit of the exertion and preparation and <span class="h">ratzon</span> alone — that we yearn for Your service and toil with many exertions — even though we have not yet merited true <span class="h">avodah</span> — through this alone may we overcome all obstacles, the aspect of jackals and shadow of death.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"Many waters cannot extinguish the love."</span> Many waters — the nations and <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> from which all obstacles come — cannot extinguish the love and <span class="h">ratzon</span>. For we are great stubborn people in <span class="h">ratzon</span>. The more obstacles grow, the more we strengthen with stronger <span class="h">ratzonos</span>. For the obstacles' essential purpose is only to fell one from <span class="h">ratzon</span> — that is the essential test. But in truth Israel's love and <span class="h">ratzon</span> is as strong as death — matching the obstacle. <span class="v">"Many waters"</span> — the obstacles — cannot extinguish the love and <span class="h">ratzon</span>; on the contrary, we strengthen with ever stronger <span class="h">ratzon</span> and wondrous desire, for the obstacle exists for the desire. Therefore we will certainly accomplish what we desire — to draw close to Hashem. Hashem will always take pride in us: <span class="v">"set me as a seal,"</span> as above.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 21 — "<i>Sit at My Right</i>": Love and Desire Defeat the Enemies</div>

<div class="p">This is <span class="v">"sit at My right until I make your enemies a footstool for your feet."</span> The right is the aspect of love and desire. Through this, the essential overcoming of enemies and foes — the obstacles. This is <span class="v">"upon the lion and cobra you shall tread, you shall trample the young lion and serpent — for he has desired Me, and I will deliver him."</span> Lion, cobra, young lion, serpent — <span class="h">kelipos</span> and <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>, obstacles spreading across the holy path like snakes and lions, not allowing anyone to walk the holy path. The verse promises the Jew: he can tread upon them and trample them through <span class="h">ratzon</span> and desire — <span class="v">"for he has desired [chashak] Me and I will deliver him"</span> — <span class="v">"chashak"</span> specifically — the essential overcoming is through desire and <span class="h">ratzon</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore before <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>, when one must reveal the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> to draw <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, one says <span class="h">Birchas HaZimun</span> — <span class="v">"let us bless [the One] from Whose [bounty] we have eaten"</span> — preparation and invitation to the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> we wish to fulfill. This is <span class="h">ratzon</span> and yearning — we declare with our mouths that we wish to fulfill His <span class="h">mitzvos</span> — <span class="v">"let us bless."</span> This is the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, for its essence is <span class="h">ratzon</span>. Through this the essential <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> is revealed — the essential <span class="h">mitzvah</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>.</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of saying before every <span class="h">mitzvah</span>: <span class="mx">"I am prepared and ready to fulfill the mitzvah of tefillin"</span> or <span class="h">tzitzis</span>, etc. This is <span class="h">ratzon</span> — we declare and reveal our strong desire to fulfill His <span class="h">mitzvos</span>. We have no power to fulfill them properly — we only say we are prepared and ready — this is <span class="h">ratzon</span>. Then the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> is accomplished of itself with Hashem's help, for <span class="mx">"one who comes to purify is assisted."</span> Everything is from Him. Our essential <span class="h">avodah</span> is the <span class="h">ratzon</span> — the aspect of "I am prepared and ready."</div>

<div class="p">Since at the time of eating one must reveal the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — through which the essential <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> and holiness of eating [are achieved] — and at the time of eating is the height of battle (for the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> <span class="mx">"stands at a person's table to prosecute,"</span> as stated in the holy Zohar, wanting to prevail and nullify the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>) — therefore our Sages established <span class="h">Birchas HaZimun</span>. Through the invitation to <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>, which is the <span class="h">ratzon</span>, one overcomes the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> and reveals the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> — for the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is in <span class="h">ratzon</span>. Through this one draws <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> — the essential <span class="h">mitzvah</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>. As also explained in the <span class="h">kavanos</span>: through the invitation to a holy <span class="h">mitzvah</span>, the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> is driven away — the invitation is <span class="h">ratzon</span>, through which the essential overcoming.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 22 — <i>Zimun</i> Requires Three: <i>Tiferes</i> and <i>Kedushah Meshuleshes</i></div>

<div class="p">Therefore the essential <span class="h">Birchas HaZimun</span> is with three. When three Jews are present, there is the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>. For the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is in the aspect of Yaakov, who is <span class="h">Tiferes</span>, as is known. Yaakov is the third of the <span class="h">Avos</span>, comprised of all three. All Israel are called by the name Yaakov, who is called Yisrael — there the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>: <span class="v">"Yisrael, in whom I take pride."</span></div>

<div class="p">This is <span class="h">Kedushah Meshuleshes</span> [triple sanctification]. For the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is the aspect of <span class="h">tefillin</span> — <span class="h">mochin</span> called <span class="h">Kodesh</span>, as is known — <span class="v">"engraved like a seal: Holy to Hashem."</span> The essential holiness is the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>: <span class="v">"and I will be magnified and sanctified."</span> The magnification of His Name — the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, His honor and greatness — <span class="v">"the preciousness of His majestic glory"</span> — is His essential holiness: <span class="v">"and I will be magnified and sanctified"</span> — His Name is magnified and sanctified through the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> received from Israel. The <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is the totality of colors, and the essential colors are the three colors of the eye that illuminate the pupil — the holiness of Israel, comprised of three <span class="h">Avos</span>, the three colors of the eye through which the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>. Therefore holiness is triple, for <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is holiness. The <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> through Torah-fulfillment — Torah is in all its aspects triple: <span class="mx">"Blessed is the Merciful One who gave a threefold Torah through a third [Moshe] on the third day"</span> (Shabbos 88). Therefore <span class="h">Birchas HaZimun</span>, where the essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is revealed, requires three — the aspect of three <span class="h">Avos</span>, three colors, triple holiness. Then the essential obligation of the cup of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> [applies], for the cup is the revelation of <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> revealed specifically in three. This is the aspect of the three <span class="h">berachos</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 23 — Three <i>Shabbos</i> Meals</div>

<div class="p">This is the three meals of <span class="h">Shabbos</span>. The essential revelation of <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, is on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>, when all <span class="h">mitzvos</span> ascend before Hashem and He takes pride in them, as Rabbainu writes on <span class="v">"righteousness walks before him"</span> (<span class="lr">Siman 277</span>). Therefore then the faces shine with supernal radiance through the light of Israel's <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>. The essential revelation of <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is through the <span class="h">tzadik</span>, the aspect of Moshe. This is <span class="v">"a crown of glory [tiferes] You placed upon him"</span> — said on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>. And <span class="v">"who is like Your nation Israel, one nation in the land — glory of greatness [tiferes gedulah]."</span> The essential <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>. Therefore it is a great <span class="h">mitzvah</span> to eat the <span class="h">Shabbos</span> meal, for <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is revealed at holy eating, which is <span class="h">Shabbos</span> eating. Therefore one must eat three meals on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>, for <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> is comprised of three. These three colors, the totality of <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, illuminate the pupil — the aspect of the cup of blessing, <span class="h">Malchus</span> of Dovid, <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> that receives all the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, from which its essential holiness. This is <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> by three over the cup — the essential completeness of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>, when <span class="h">zimun</span> by three over the cup reveals the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, the essential <span class="h">mitzvah</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 24 — Avraham: The First to Reveal <i>Eretz Yisrael</i> Through <i>Ratzon</i></div>

<div class="p">Therefore Avraham was the first to reveal the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, as stated in the Zohar and mentioned in our words many times. For Avraham was the first generous heart [<span class="h">nediv lev</span>]. His entire <span class="h">avodah</span> was only <span class="h">ratzon</span> and <span class="h">kisufin</span> of holiness, as explained elsewhere. For he lived before <span class="h">Matan Torah</span>. At the beginning of his <span class="h">avodah</span> he did not know of any <span class="h">mitzvah</span>. His entire <span class="h">avodah</span> was only <span class="h">ratzon</span> and desire and <span class="h">kisufin</span> of holiness. He was strong and fierce in <span class="h">ratzon</span> greatly — against the entire world that stood against him to prevent him. Through this he merited to break all enemies and obstacles — the aspect of <span class="v">"sit at My right until I make your enemies a footstool"</span> — said regarding Avraham. Through all this, Hashem took great pride in him: <span class="v">"Avraham, My beloved."</span> Through this he merited to reveal the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, for its holiness is revealed through the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> whose essence is through <span class="h">ratzon</span>, as above.</div>

<div class="p">Through the greatness of his desire and good <span class="h">ratzon</span> — in which he was very fierce and strong — he merited the revelation of the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> of <span class="h">milah</span>, which is <span class="h">tikkun habris</span>. Through this the essential breaking of the <span class="h">azus</span> of the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>, from which all obstacles come, and one merits holy <span class="h">azus</span>, which depends on the holiness of the <span class="h">bris</span> — <span class="mx">"in it is strength, in it is might,"</span> as is known. He merited to bear Yitzchak, the first born in the holiness of Israel, from whom joy and <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span> of holiness began. Therefore he is named for laughter and joy: <span class="v">"G-d has made laughter for me."</span> For the essential joy is through the <span class="h">his'pa'arus</span>, as above.</div>

<div class="ts">
<div class="sh">✦ Summary — BhM Halachah 4 Complete ✦</div>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>Core teaching</strong> (<span class="lr">LM II:40</span>): <em>His'pa'arus</em> → eyes of Hashem → <em>Eretz Yisrael</em>. The <em>tzadik</em> embodies all the <em>his'pa'arus</em>; gazing at him on <em>Rosh HaShanah</em> creates <em>Eretz Yisrael</em> everywhere.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>Practical halachos</strong>: Cup of <em>Birchas HaMazon</em> = gaze at it (§§1-3). Don't eat before praying (§4). <em>Seudos mitzvah</em>, <em>Shabbos/Yom Tov</em> eating (§§6-7). Chanukah candle — gaze at it, three levels of lighting (§§9-11). <em>Menorah mikshah</em> = stubbornness (§12). Eight days = eight garments of <em>Kohain Gadol</em> (§15). <em>Parshas Mikaitz</em> on Chanukah (§16). <em>Tzedakah</em> on Chanukah breaks money-desire (§§17-19). <em>Birchas HaZimun</em> in three = <em>ratzon</em> (§§20-22). Three <em>Shabbos</em> meals (§23).</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>Central message</strong>: The essential <em>avodah</em> is <em>ratzon</em>. Even if one cannot break the obstacles, the <em>ratzon</em> alone is the essential <em>his'pa'arus</em>. "Love is as strong as death" — never abandon the <em>ratzon</em>. Through <em>ratzon</em> alone, all obstacles eventually transform into salvations.</p>
</div>

